  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: d01fd2d64a9249049aaa77d5c12a82fe, type: 3}
  m_Name: Question1
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  questionText: Calculate the density of species C in the given quadrats. Quadrat-I
    shows the counts of species A - 5, species B-3, species C- 10; Quadrat- Il shows,
    species A - 3, species B- 5, species C-4. Density of species C will be_
  referenceImage: {fileID: 0}
  explanationText: The number of sample areas (Q) are 2 and the total population
    of species C is 14. Hence, The density of species C is derive d from above quadrats
    is 07. Density is calculated as the number of individuals (S) of the plant species
    C divided by the total number of sample areas (Q). Density = S/Q
  options:
  - 14
  - 5
  - 7
  - 0.7
  correctOptionIndex: 2
